    "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements **ADR-028: CSS Grid Layout (Basic)** — `display: grid` + fixed/fr tracks + `minmax` + named areas + gaps. Four commits.\n\n**Unusual framing**: the biggest deliverable in this PR wasn't grid layout. It's a **root-relative URL resolution bug** discovered during grid verification that had been silently 404ing every external CSS fetch since ADR-025. That means ADR-025/026/027's verified deltas were inline-only; external CSS never actually loaded. Post-fix, all three prior ADRs' features reach the cascade for the first time.\n\nGrid layout itself is real and works (sidebar narrows to a left column, article indents), but has a deferred vertical-positioning bug. The URL fix is what actually unblocks the whole arc.\n\n## The URL fix (the biggest deliverable, discovered during grid verification)\n\n### The bug\n\n`resolve_url(\"/path\", base)` was concatenating root-relative hrefs onto the base URL's **directory** (with subdirectories) instead of its **origin** (scheme + host):\n\n```\nBefore: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML + /w/load.php\n      → https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/w/load.php   (404)\n\nAfter:  https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTML + /w/load.php\n      → https://en.wikipedia.org/w/load.php         (correct)\n```\n\n### The consequence\n\n**Every external CSS fetch on Wikipedia has been silently 404ing since ADR-025.** Wikipedia's external CSS hrefs are root-relative (`/w/load.php?...`) and its base URL has a `/wiki/` subdirectory — exactly the shape that triggers the bug.\n\nADR-025, ADR-026, and ADR-027 all verified real visible deltas on Wikipedia. **Those deltas were real — but from inline `<style>` tags** (Wikipedia's TemplateStyles extension emits ~20KB of inline CSS in `<body>`), **not from external CSS.** The 222KB of external CSS that ADR-025 was supposed to be loading never reached the cascade.\n\nPost-fix, it does.\n\n### Why every prior test missed it\n\nEvery URL-resolution test used a base URL **without a subdirectory** (`https://example.com/page.html`). The `dir == origin` case produces identical results, masking the bug. Only a base URL with a subdirectory exposes it.\n\n### The fix\n\n`resolve_url` splits the base at the first `/` after the scheme separator to get the origin, then concatenates the href onto scheme + host + port. Falls back gracefully for scheme-less bases and preserves ports.\n\n### Post-fix corrections to ADR-025/026/027\n\nEach of ADR-025, ADR-026, and ADR-027 gets a \"Post-ADR-028 correction\" section appended. Their measured deltas were **inline-only**; post-fix, their actual capability is larger than measured at the time. Historical record preserved rather than rewritten.\n\n## What grid layout actually ships\n\n### Working\n\n- `display: grid` parses to `Display::Grid`.\n- `grid-template-columns` / `grid-template-rows`: fixed (rem/px), `Nfr`, `minmax(0 | length, Nfr | length)`, `min-content`/`max-content`/`auto`.\n- `grid-template-areas`: named cell map with spanning support (`'siteNotice siteNotice'` → col_span = 2) and `.` empty cells.\n- Per-child `grid-area` placement.\n- `column-gap` / `row-gap`.\n- `grid-template` shorthand expansion.\n- `shift_subtree_y` for placing children at row Y positions after natural layout.\n\n### Measured visible delta on Wikipedia (viewport 1774)\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Sidebar narrows to ~325px left column | ✅ |\n| Article content indents to right column | ✅ |\n| Navbox styling preserved (ADR-027) | ✅ |\n| Article body readable | ✅ |\n| **Article's vertical position within cell** | ❌ ~660px too low (deferred) |\n| No crash, no regression | ✅ |\n\n**The structural transform (columns side by side) DID happen.** \"HTML\" heading is at x≈325 (right column), article body indented correctly. The article's vertical placement within its cell is offset by ~660px — heading at y≈730 instead of y≈70.\n\n### Deferred vertical positioning bug\n\nRoot cause hypothesis (unverified — needs another diagnostic round):\n- (a) the article's `.mw-content-container` contains block children before its visible content, or\n- (b) its own internal layout adds top margin/padding not accounted for by grid row layout, or\n- (c) grid's row height calculation adds an offset.\n\nDeferred to a small follow-up commit or its own ADR. The columns work; the vertical refinement within the cell is what's missing.\n\n## Commits\n\n| Commit | Scope |\n|---|---|\n| `826e9ef` | `Display::Grid` + `display_of` + `grid-template` shorthand expansion. 14 tests. |\n| `da3def2` | **URL fix** (root-relative resolution). 4 regression tests. |\n| `de48ba2` | `grid_layout.{hpp,cpp}` + `layout_element` dispatch + `shift_subtree_y`. 23+2 tests. |\n| `5c2ee81` | Docs: ADR-028 status → Implemented, post-fix corrections to ADR-025/026/027, README, CHANGELOG. |\n\n## Test count\n\n- Before ADR-028: 327 cases, 1367 assertions\n- After Commit 1: 336 cases, 1401 assertions\n- After Commit 2a: **365 cases, 1508 assertions**\n- After Commit 3: 365 cases, 1508 assertions (unchanged, docs only)\n- Zero warnings, zero failures\n\n## Verification checklist\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `display: grid` parses | ✅ |\n| Track sizing (fixed/fr/minmax/auto) | ✅ (23 unit tests) |\n| Named areas + spanning cells | ✅ |\n| Per-child `grid-area` placement | ✅ |\n| 2-column end-to-end grid layout | ✅ |\n| Grid without template falls back to block | ✅ |\n| **URL fix: subdirectory bases resolve correctly** | ✅ (4 tests) |\n| External CSS actually reaches cascade on Wikipedia | ✅ |\n| **Sidebar narrows at 1120+ viewport** | ✅ |\n| Article content indents | ✅ |\n| **Article vertical position in cell** | ❌ deferred |\n\n## Not included (deferred)\n\n**Grid features** (0 uses on Wikipedia's page layout):\n- `inline-grid`, `subgrid`, `repeat()`, `auto`, `max-content`, `fit-content()`\n- `grid-auto-*`, line-based `grid-column`/`grid-row`\n- `fr` rows filling container height (flow-layout constraint)\n- Nested grids (untested against deep DOM)\n\n**Bugs**:\n- Article vertical position within cell (~660px off)\n\n**Followup ADRs**:\n- ADR-029 (flex layout): header bar, TOC alignment.\n- ADR-030 (position + float): overlays, thumbnails, content-embedded elements.\n\n## The arc's honest state\n\n| ADR | Delivered | Honest caveat |\n|---|---|---|\n| 025 | External CSS loading | **Actually worked inline-only pre-URL-fix; corrected post-ADR-028** |\n| 026 | var() resolution + display:none fix | Same as 025 — inline-only pre-fix |\n| 027 | @media parsing + cascade filtering | Same as 025 — inline-only pre-fix |\n| **028** | Grid layout + URL fix | Grid: partial (columns work, vertical offset). **URL fix: unblocks all prior ADRs** |\n\nThe pattern this session earned is now fully visible: **measure, ship, document honestly, correct the record when a later ADR finds an earlier measurement was measuring the wrong thing.** ADR-028's PR is the first one where a prior ADR's historical claims get explicitly corrected — that's not a regression, it's the process working.\n\n## ADR\n\n`docs/decisions/028-grid-layout.md` — status now **Implemented**, with Implementation section documenting the delta, the URL bug discovery, and the deferred vertical positioning. Plus post-fix correction sections in ADR-025, ADR-026, ADR-027.\n\nRefs #159\n",
